1.4 Tensor elements access
==========================

The functions for accessing the elements of a tensor use the GSL range
checking system.  You can turn off range checking by recompiling your
program with the preprocessor definition ‘GSL_RANGE_CHECK_OFF’.

   Tensor elements are stored in "C-order", i.e., the last index moves
continuously through memory.  For a tensor ‘t’ of ‘dim’ 3, the element
accessed at indices ‘i, j, k’ is:

t->data[i * stride[0] + j * stride[1] + k * stride[2]].

 -- Function: double tensor_get (const tensor * t, ...)

     This function returns the element specified by the indices in the
     variable argument list.  If any of the indices are out of the
     allowed range for their dimension ‘d’ of ‘0’ to ‘size[d] - 1’, then
     the error handler is invoked and ‘0’ is returned.

 -- Function: void tensor_set (const tensor * t, const double x, ...)

     This function sets the value of the element of tensor ‘t’ at the
     indices given in the variable argument list to ‘x’.  If any of the
     indices are out of the allowed range for their dimension ‘d’ of ‘0’
     to ‘size[d] - 1’, then the error handler is invoked.

 -- Function: double * tensor_ptr (tensor * t, ...)

 -- Function: const double * tensor_const_ptr (const tensor * t, ...)

     These functions return a pointer to the element of tensor ‘t’ at
     the indices given in the variable argument list.  If any of the
     indices are out of the allowed range for their dimension ‘d’ of ‘0’
     to ‘size[d] - 1’, then the error handler is invoked and a null
     pointer is returned.

 -- Function: size_t tensor_index (const tensor * t, const size_t i)

     This function returns the index ‘idx’ of the ‘i’-th consecutive
     element (as in a flat "C-order" layout) of tensor ‘t’ taking into
     account strides, such that ‘t->data[idx]’ gives the value of the
     ‘i’-th element of ‘t’.

 -- Function: double * tensor_ptr_idx (tensor * t, const size_t idx)

 -- Function: const double * tensor_const_ptr_idx (const tensor * t,
          const size_t idx)

     These are convenience functions that return a pointer to the
     tensor's element at index ‘idx’ (as obtained from ‘tensor_index
     (const tensor * t, const size_t i)’ function).  An inline version
     of these functions is used when ‘HAVE_INLINE’ is defined.


