1.7 Tensor views
================

Tensor views provide access to whole or part of the data owned by
another tensor.  Unlike GSL vector and matrix views, tensor views are
allocated from heap memory as a consequence of the arbitrary dimension
of tensors.  Therefore, it is the user's responsibility to free the
bookkeeping memory used by tensor views when the view is no longer
needed.  There is no separate type for views.  Except of not owning the
data, as indicated by the ‘owner’ field set to ‘0’, tensor views do not
differ from ordinary tensors.

 -- Function: tensor * tensor_view (tensor * t, ...)

 -- Function: const tensor * tensor_const_view (const tensor * t, ...)

     These functions return a tensor view of a sub-tensor of tensor ‘t’.
     The variable argument list should contain triplets of ‘offset,
     size, step’ for each tensor dimension, where ‘offset’ indicates the
     number of parts starting from the initial part of the dimension,
     ‘size’ is the number of parts in the resulting tensor view, and
     ‘step’ is the step-size for the dimension from the original tensor.

     A convenience macro ‘RANGE (start, end, step)’ defined in ‘range.h’
     can be used to form a triplet for a dimension in the previous
     functions.  It accepts a ‘start’ and ‘end’ index for the parts of
     the original tensor dimension and a step-size.

 -- Function: tensor * tensor_view_array (double * array, const size_t
          dim, ...)

 -- Function: const tensor * tensor_const_view_array (const double *
          array, const size_t dim, ...)

     These functions return a tensor view of the array ‘array’.  The
     variable argument list should contain the sizes for each dimension.
     The original array should not be deallocated while the view is
     still in use.

   The following functions provide conversions between GSL vector and
matrix to tensor and vice-versa for tensors of dimensions one and two.

 -- Function: tensor * tensor_view_vector (gsl_vector * vector)

 -- Function: const tensor * tensor_const_view_vector (const gsl_vector
          * vector)

     These functions return a tensor view from a GSL vector ‘vector’.

 -- Function: gsl_vector_view gsl_vector_view_tensor (tensor * t)

 -- Function: gsl_vector_const_view gsl_vector_const_view_tensor (const
          tensor * t)

     These functions return a GSL vector view from a tensor ‘t’.

 -- Function: tensor * tensor_view_matrix (gsl_matrix * matrix)

 -- Function: const tensor * tensor_const_view_matrix (const gsl_matrix
          * matrix)

     These functions return a tensor view from a GSL matrix ‘matrix’.

 -- Function: gsl_matrix_view gsl_matrix_view_tensor (tensor * t)

 -- Function: gsl_matrix_const_view gsl_matrix_const_view_tensor (const
          tensor * t)

     These functions return a GSL matrix view from a tensor ‘t’.


