1.8.4 Trigonometric operators
-----------------------------

The functions below are defined for floating-point data type tensors.
From the complex tensors, only the ‘double’ data type is supported.

 -- Function: void tensor_sin (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the sine of the elements in ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_cos (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the cosine of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_tan (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the tangent of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_sec (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the secant of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_csc (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the cosecant of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_cot (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the cotangent of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_arcsin (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the arcsine of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_arccos (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the arccosine of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: void tensor_arctan (tensor * t)

     This functions calculates inplace the arctangent of the elements in
     ‘t’.

 -- Function: tensor * tensor_arctan2 (const tensor * y, const tensor *
          x)

     This function returns a tensor containing the computation of the
