1.8.9 Logical operators
-----------------------

 -- Function: void tensor_not (tensor * t)

     This function performs a negation (logical not) operation on each
     element in tensor ‘t’.

 -- Function: tensor_int * tensor_fcmp (const tensor * t1, const tensor
          * t2, const double eps)

     This function determines whether elements in tensor ‘t1’ are
     approximately equal to a relative accuracy ‘eps’ to corresponding
     elements in tensor ‘t2’.  It returns an ‘int’ tensor with values
     ‘-1’ where the element in ‘t1’ is less that the one in ‘t2’, ‘0’
     where they are approximately equal, and ‘1’ where it is greater.
     It is based on the ‘gsl_fcmp’ function.  *Note (gsl-ref)Approximate
     Comparison of Floating Point Numbers::.

 -- Function: tensor_int * tensor_fcmpc (const tensor * t, const double
          x, const double eps)

     This function determines whether elements in tensor ‘t’ are
     approximately equal to a relative accuracy ‘eps’ to a constant
     value ‘x’.  It returns an ‘int’ tensor with values ‘-1’ where the
     element in ‘t1’ is less that the one in ‘t2’, ‘0’ where they are
     approximately equal, and ‘1’ where it is greater.  It is based on
     the ‘gsl_fcmp’ function.  *Note (gsl-ref)Approximate Comparison of
     Floating Point Numbers::.

 -- Function: tensor_int * tensor_cmp (const tensor * t1, const tensor *
          t2)

     This function performs a comparison operation between the elements
     in tensors ‘t1’ and ‘t2’.  It returns an int tensor with element
     values ‘-1’ where an element in tensor ‘t1’ is less than that of
     ‘t2’, ‘0’ where it is equal, and ‘1’ where it is larger.  The input
     tensors need to have matching sizes.

 -- Function: tensor_int * tensor_cmpc (const tensor * t, const double *
          x)

     This function performs a comparison operation between the elements
     in tensors ‘t’ and a constant value ‘x’.  It returns an int tensor
     with element values ‘-1’ where an element in tensor ‘t1’ is less
     than ‘x’, ‘0’ where it is equal, and ‘1’ where it is larger.

 -- Function: tensor_int * tensor_and (const tensor * t1, const tensor *
          t2)

     This function performs a logical ‘and’ operation between the
     elements in tensors ‘t1’ and ‘t2’.  It returns an ‘int’ tensor with
     element values ‘1’ where both elements in ‘t1’ and ‘t2’ evaluate to
     true, and ‘0’ otherwise.  The input tensors need to have matching
     sizes.

 -- Function: tensor_int * tensor_or (const tensor * t1, const tensor *
          t2)

     This function performs a logical ‘or’ operation between the
     elements in tensors ‘t1’ and ‘t2’.  It returns an ‘int’ tensor with
     element values ‘1’ where at least one element in ‘t1’ or ‘t2’
     evaluates to true, and ‘0’ otherwise.  The input tensors need to
     have matching sizes.

 -- Function: tensor_int * tensor_xor (const tensor * t1, const tensor *
          t2)

     This function performs a logical ‘xor’ operation between the
     elements in tensors ‘t1’ and ‘t2’.  It returns an ‘int’ tensor with
     element values ‘1’ where at most one of the elements, either in
     ‘t1’ or ‘t2’, evaluates to true, and ‘0’ otherwise.  The input
     tensors need to have matching sizes.


