1.8.10 Sorting operators
------------------------

These functions sort tensor data, either directly or indirectly by using
an index.  All the functions rely on the heapsort algorithm as
implemented in GSL.

 -- Function: void tensor_sort (tensor * t)

     This function sorts the elements of tensor ‘t’ inplace into
     ascending order.

 -- Function: void tensor_sort_index (size_t * p, const tensor * t)

     This function indirectly sorts the elements of tensor ‘t’ into
     ascending order.  The resulting permutation is stored in array ‘p’,
     which should be of size equal to the total number of elements in
     ‘t’.  The elements of ‘p’ give the index of the tensor element
     which would have been stored in that position if the tensor had
     been sorted in place.  The first element of ‘p’ gives the index of
     the smallest element in ‘t’, and the last element of ‘p’ gives the
     index of the greatest element in ‘t’.  The tensor itself is not
     changed.


