1.9 Tensor properties
=====================

These functions below are defined for both real and complex tensors.
For complex tensors, both the real and the imaginary part must satisfy
the conditions for ‘is_null, is_pos, is_neg, is_nonneg, is_nonpos’
functions.

 -- Function: int tensor_match_size (const tensor * t1, const tensor *
          t2)

     This functions compares the dimensions and sizes of tensors ‘t1’
     and ‘t2’.  It returns ‘1’ if the dimensions and the sizes match,
     otherwise, it signals an error ‘GSL_EBADLEN’ and returns ‘0’.

 -- Function: int tensor_match_tsize (const tensor * t1, const tensor *
          t2)

     This functions compares the total number of elements of tensors
     ‘t1’ and ‘t2’.  It returns ‘1’ if they are equal, otherwise, it
     signals an error ‘GSL_EBADLEN’ and returns ‘0’.

 -- Function: int tensor_is_null (const tensor * t)

 -- Function: int tensor_is_pos (const tensor * t)

 -- Function: int tensor_is_neg (const tensor * t)

 -- Function: int tensor_is_nonneg (const tensor * t)

 -- Function: int tensor_is_nonpos (const tensor * t)

     These functions return ‘1’ if all of the elements of tensor ‘t’ are
     null, positive, negative, non-negative, non-positive respectively,
     and ‘0’ otherwise.

 -- Function: int tensor_equal (const tensor * t1, const tensor * t2)

     This function returns ‘1’ if each of the elements of tensor ‘t1’ is
     equal to the corresponding element of tensor ‘t2’, and ‘0’
     otherwise.

 -- Function: int tensor_is_same (const tensor * t)

     This function returns ‘1’ if tensor ‘t’ has same (identical) values
     for each element, and ‘0’ otherwise.

 -- Function: int tensor_is_const (const tensor * t, const double c)

     This function returns ‘1’ if tensor ‘t’ has all elements equal to a
     constant ‘c’, and ‘0’ otherwise.

 -- Function: size_t tensor_tsize (const tensor * t)

     This function return the total number of elements in tensor ‘t’.
     An inline version of this function is used when ‘HAVE_INLINE’ is
     defined.

 -- Function: int tensor_is_view (const tensor * t)

     This function returns ‘1’ if tensor ‘t’ is a view, and ‘0’
     otherwise.  An inline version of this function is used when
     ‘HAVE_INLINE’ is defined.

 -- Function: int tensor_is_contiguous (const tensor * t)

     This function returns ‘1’ if tensor ‘t’'s memory is contiguous, and
     ‘0’ otherwise.  An inline version of this function is used when
     ‘HAVE_INLINE’ is defined.


